Implement `ITEM-001-player-selector` in all relevant screens.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Six selectable, serializable player colours are available.
- [x] The selector shows "Player:" followed by all six player colours in one row.
- [x] The selected colour contains a visible tick and tapping another colour selects it immediately.
- [x] Selection is shared between the Board and Plan Browser screens.
- [x] Roads and buildings are stored and rendered in their owning player's colour.
- [x] Players cannot modify pieces owned by another player.
- [x] Placeholder plan statistics update for the selected player.
- [x] The selector has a stable footprint and does not reflow surrounding content when selection changes.
- [x] Should only be visible on `SCR-001-board` when in edit mode.
- [x] On Board it appears below Terrain/Numbers; in Plans it appears below Default/Custom.
- [ ] Relevant automated checks pass.

## Implementation notes

- `PlayerColor` defines the six serializable players and their stable display order.
- `PlayerSelector` is a reusable binding-based horizontal control used by Board, Plan Browser, and plan editing.
- The current ITEM-001 design exposes every player at once; it has no collapsed/expanded state or navigation-title side effect.
- Screens present the selector over a fixed-height footprint. Board only presents it while editing.
- Board and Plans place the selector in normal layout beneath their respective segmented controls.
- `BoardSnapshot` retains its existing road/building collections and adds ownership maps, with missing ownership decoded as Red for backward compatibility.
- Structural editing receives the selected player; occupied pieces owned by another player are left unchanged.
- All six player profiles vary plan timing and recompute internally consistent summary statistics and monotonic probability curves until the simulation backend replaces them.

## Evidence

- Added domain tests for six-player serialization, ownership, isolation, and snapshot round trips.
- Added plan tests confirming all six profiles have distinct means, ordered percentiles, and monotonic probability curves without changing plan definitions.
- Added UI coverage confirming all choices share one row, the selected tick state, stable surrounding frames, edit-only Board visibility, and shared state in Plans.
- The latest selector and stable Board layout compile in the app and both test bundles using `/private/tmp/Catanalyst-selector-position-derived`.
- UI coverage compares selector/control frames to verify the required vertical ordering.
- `xcodebuild build-for-testing -quiet -project Catanalyst.xcodeproj -scheme Catanalyst -destination 'generic/platform=iOS Simulator' -derivedDataPath /private/tmp/Catanalyst-task007-derived` succeeded for the app and both test bundles after the horizontal overlay and profile changes.

## Remaining risks and manual checks

- Execute the focused domain and UI tests after CoreSimulator provides a concrete destination.
- Manually confirm the six-colour row and tick contrast, shared selection, and player-owned road/building editing.
